-- title:
--   Injective morphisms reflect the deformation-condition subfunctor
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative local ring whose residue field is finite, and let $\mathcal{D}$ be a predicate assigning to every commutative local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $A$ and every rank-two adically continuous Galois representation $\rho \in$ [`GaloisRepAdic A`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16) (a finite free $A$-module $V$ of rank $2$ together with a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, realised as $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, to $\mathrm{End}_A(V)$ acting trivially modulo $\mathfrak{m}_A^n$ on the Galois group of a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, for each $n$) a truth value. Let $\rho_0$ be a continuous homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, taken with the discrete topology. Assume $\mathcal{D}$ is a deformation condition in the sense of [`GaloisRep.IsDeformationCondition`](def/GaloisRep_DeformationCondition.html#L19): on Artinian test algebras it is invariant under isomorphism of representations and stable under base change along local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra maps, it descends along injective local maps and along fibre-product presentations, and for Noetherian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebras that are complete for the maximal-adic topology and have residue field generated by $\mathcal{O}$ it holds exactly when it holds for all base changes along surjective local maps onto Artinian test algebras. Then the subfunctor [`GaloisRep.conditionSubfunctor 𝒪 𝒟 ρ₀`](def/GaloisRep_ConditionLifts.html#L22) of the framed-representation functor $A \mapsto \{$continuous homomorphisms $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(A)\}$ on local pro-Artinian $\mathcal{O}$-algebras, whose value at $A$ is the predicate `conditionLifts 𝒪 𝒟 ρ₀ A` selecting those representations which lift $\rho_0$ along the terminal morphism to the residue field and for which $\mathcal{D}$ holds on the realisations obtained from morphisms out of $A$, is reflected by injective morphisms: for every morphism $\iota : T \to A$ of local pro-Artinian $\mathcal{O}$-algebras with injective underlying map and every continuous $\sigma : \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(T)$, if the push-forward of $\sigma$ along $\iota$ lies in the subfunctor at $A$, then $\sigma$ lies in it at $T$.
--
--   This is the descent-along-subobjects property of Mazur's deformation conditions, transported from representations to the framed-lift subfunctor they cut out. It is used in the construction of the data attached to the deformation ring of $\rho_0$ of type $\mathcal{D}$, being cited by [`GaloisRep.nonempty_deformationRingData`](thm.html#GaloisRep.nonempty_deformationRingData).
